{"parse":{"title":"2026–27 UEFA Nations League B","pageid":72856419,"revid":1382087408,"redirects":[],"wikitext":"{{Use dmy dates|date=February 2026}}\n{{Infobox international football competition\n| tourney_name   = UEFA Nations League B\n| year           = 2026–27\n| dates          = 24 September – 17 November 2026\n| num_teams      = 16\n| promoted       =\n| relegated      =\n| matches        = 32\n| goals          = 71\n| attendance     = {{#invoke:Football attendance summation|main|groups=leagueb}}\n| top_scorer     = {{fbicon|IRL}} [[Troy Parrott]]<br>{{fbicon|SWE}} [[Viktor Gyökeres]]<br>(4 goals each)\n| prevseason     = [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League B|2024–25]]\n| updated        = 6 October 2026\n| nextseason     = ''2028–29''\n}}\nThe '''2026–27 UEFA Nations League B''' is the second division of the [[2026–27 UEFA Nations League|2026–27 edition]] of the [[UEFA Nations League]], the fifth season of the international [[Association football|football]] competition involving the men's national teams of the member associations of [[UEFA]].\n\n==Format==\nLeague B consists of 16 UEFA members ranked from 17–32 in the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League#Final overall ranking|2024–25 UEFA Nations League final overall ranking]], split into four groups of four. Each team will play six matches within their group, using the home-and-away [[round-robin tournament|round-robin]] format on matchdays in September, October and November 2026.<ref name=\"need to know\">{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefanationsleague/news/0298-1d6ef1acfaef-b54fcf1da859-1000/ |title=2026/27 UEFA Nations League: All you need to know |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=9 February 2026 |access-date=11 February 2026}}</ref> The winners of each group will be promoted to the [[2028–29 UEFA Nations League#League A|2028–29 UEFA Nations League A]]. In addition, the second-placed teams of each group will participate in [[2026–27 UEFA Nations League promotion/relegation play-offs|promotion play-offs]] against a third or fourth-placed team from [[2026–27 UEFA Nations League A|League A]], while the League B fourth-placed teams will participate in relegation play-offs against the second-placed teams from [[2026–27 UEFA Nations League C|League C]], both taking place in March 2027. In the play-offs, teams from the higher leagues will host the second leg, with the winners of each tie participating in the higher league for the next Nations League season, while the losers will enter the lower league.<ref name=\"regulations\">{{cite web |url=https://documents.uefa.com/r/Regulations-of-the-UEFA-Nations-League-2026/27-Online |title=Regulations of the UEFA Nations League 2026/27 |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=December 2025 |access-date=13 December 2025 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260211170553/https://documents.uefa.com/api/khub/maps/HlG1NvOr4H_30IjSKzlRKg/attachments/2b1W4zSbckOh3ZMUhu0_wg-HlG1NvOr4H_30IjSKzlRKg/content |archive-date=11 February 2026}}</ref>\n\nOriginally, the format for promotion and relegation would have involved only the last-placed teams in Leagues A and B being relegated. The promotion/relegation play-offs would have concerned all third-placed teams in Leagues A and B and all runners-up in Leagues B and C, with extra play-offs concerning the two best last-places in League C to be held in March 2028. However, due to the [[UEFA Nations League#Post-2028 review and proposed format changes|changes scheduled for the 2028–29 UEFA Nations League]], in which the competition will be reduced from four leagues to three leagues of 18 teams, promotion/relegation was rebalanced to make all three upcoming leagues be at 18 teams.<ref>{{cite web |date=15 September 2026 |title=New promotion/relegation system for UEFA Nations League 2026/27 |url=https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/02a9-21985b7e3370-3f0fda209606-1000/promotion_and_relegation_unl_website.pdf |access-date=18 September 2026 |publisher=[[UEFA]]}}</ref>\n\n==Teams==\nLeague B includes sixteen teams based on the results of the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League|2024–25 season]]: the four group fourth-placed teams from [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League A#Groups|League A]], the four losers of the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League promotion/relegation play-offs#League A vs League B|League A/B play-offs]], the four group winners from [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League C|League C]] and the four winners of the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League promotion/relegation play-offs#League B vs League C|League B/C play-offs]].\n\n===Team changes===\nThe following were the team changes in League B from the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League B|2024–25 season]]:<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefanationsleague/news/0292-1c2abf3ccd56-d65f5c73f690-1000/ |title=Nations League final standings: Who made the quarter-finals? Who's been promoted? Who's been relegated? Who's in the play-offs? |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=22 November 2024 |access-date=11 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefanationsleague/news/0296-1d165d4a3647-4d55eede66c2-1000/ |title=Nations League play-offs: Results, promotion and relegation |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=23 March 2025 |access-date=11 February 2026}}</ref>\n\n{|\n|- style=\"vertical-align:top\"\n|\n{| class=\"wikitable\" style=\"width:400px\"\n|+ Incoming\n|-\n! style=\"width:50%\" | Relegated from<br />[[2024–25 UEFA Nations League A|Nations League A]]\n! style=\"width:50%\" | Promoted from<br />[[2024–25 UEFA Nations League C|Nations League C]]\n|- style=\"vertical-align:top\"\n| {{Plainlist|\n* {{fb|BIH}}\n* {{fb|HUN}}\n* {{fb|ISR}} \n* {{fb|POL}}\n* {{fb|SCO}}\n* {{fb|SUI|civil}}\n}}\n| {{Plainlist|\n* {{fb|KOS}}\n* {{fb|MKD}}\n* {{fb|NIR}}\n* {{fb|ROU}}\n* {{fb|SWE}}\n}}\n|}\n|\n{| class=\"wikitable\" style=\"width:400px\"\n|+ Outgoing\n|-\n! style=\"width:50%\" | Promoted to<br />[[2026–27 UEFA Nations League A|Nations League A]]\n! style=\"width:50%\" | Relegated to<br />[[2026–27 UEFA Nations League C|Nations League C]]\n|- style=\"vertical-align:top\"\n| {{Plainlist|\n* {{fb|CZE}}\n* {{fb|ENG}}\n* {{fb|GRE}}\n* {{fb|NOR}}\n* {{fb|TUR}}\n* {{fb|WAL}}\n}}\n| {{Plainlist|\n* {{fb|ALB}}\n* {{fb|FIN}}\n* {{fb|ISL}}\n* {{fb|KAZ}}\n* {{fb|MNE}}\n}}\n|}\n|}\n\n===Seeding===\nThe teams were seeded for the league phase based on the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League#Final overall ranking|2024–25 Nations League final overall ranking]], considering promotion and relegation between the leagues.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/029a-1df96111817a-2669251e926b-1000/unl_final_overall_rankings_after_unlf_2025.pdf |title=Final overall rankings of the UEFA Nations League 2024/25 (updated following the UNL finals 2025) |publisher=[[UEFA]] |access-date=24 October 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/02a1-1fc00969b028-b36e773fcfc7-1000/20260123_circular_2026_03_en.zip |title=UEFA Nations League 2026/27 – League phase draw and fixture list procedures |number=03/2026 |magazine=UEFA Circular Letter |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=23 January 2026 |access-date=11 February 2026}}</ref>\n\n{|\n|- style=\"vertical-align:top\"\n|\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|-\n|+ Pot 1\n|-\n! width=\"190\" | Team\n! {{Tooltip|Rank|Ranking (all UEFA teams)}}\n|-\n| {{fb|SCO}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 17\n|-\n| {{fb|HUN}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 18\n|-\n| {{fb|POL}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 19\n|-\n| {{fb|ISR}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 20\n|}\n|\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|-\n|+ Pot 2\n|-\n! width=\"190\" | Team\n! {{Tooltip|Rank|Ranking (all UEFA teams)}}\n|-\n| {{fb|SUI|civil}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 21\n|-\n| {{fb|BIH}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 22\n|-\n| {{fb|AUT}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 23\n|-\n| {{fb|UKR}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 24\n|}\n|\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|-\n|+ Pot 3\n|-\n! width=\"190\" | Team\n! {{Tooltip|Rank|Ranking (all UEFA teams)}}\n|-\n| {{fb|SVN}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 25\n|-\n| {{fb|GEO}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 26\n|-\n| {{fb|IRL}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 27\n|-\n| {{fb|ROU}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 28\n|}\n|\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|-\n|+ Pot 4\n|-\n! width=\"190\" | Team\n! {{Tooltip|Rank|Ranking (all UEFA teams)}}\n|-\n| {{fb|SWE}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 29\n|-\n| {{fb|MKD}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 30\n|-\n| {{fb|NIR}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 31\n|-\n| {{fb|KOS}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 32\n|}\n|}\n\nThe draw for the league phase took place in [[Brussels]], Belgium, on 12 February 2026, 18:00 [[Central European Time|CET]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefanationsleague/draws/2027/2002276/ |title=League phase draw |publisher=[[UEFA]] |access-date=11 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefanationsleague/news/02a1-1fc60cd57c4d-de2c1d716ed6-1000/ |title=Draw for the league phase of the 2026/27 UEFA Nations League |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=11 February 2026 |access-date=11 February 2026}}</ref> Groups were drawn to contain one team from each pot. For [[Bosnia and Herzegovina–Kosovo relations|political reasons]], Bosnia and Herzegovina vs Kosovo was considered a prohibited clash, and thus those teams were unable to be drawn into the same group.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/02a2-1fe81f47532b-33ea7fae9cab-1000/20260123_circular_2026_03_en_enclosure_1_unl_2627_league_phase_draw_procedure_en_1.pdf |title=League phase draw procedure |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=12 February 2026 |access-date=13 February 2026}}</ref>\n\n==Groups==\nThe fixture list was confirmed by UEFA on 13 February 2026, the day following the draw.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefanationsleague/news/02a2-1fea18abbcbc-456e846509e7-1000/ |title=2026/27 UEFA Nations League: All the league phase fixtures |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=13 February 2026 |access-date=13 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/02a2-1fea0cbd54af-e56